<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>AdapRas: Adaptation of a raster files</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>
<body>
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
  <blockquote>
    <p>- Side.</p>

    <p>- Net.</p>

    <p>- Horizontal Reference System.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <p>The operation is made based on the relation of the three parameters described above</p>

  <blockquote>
    <p>- If the sides, mesh and geographic reference systems are equal, there is an adjustment to the envelope of the second raster. The values of the result 
	are the same as the raster to adapt, unless the scope of the raster result has no point on the raster to adapt, and in that case, the values will be equal to NoData. There is no interpolation.</p>

    <p>- If the reference systems are the same, but the sides and/or meshes are different types of adaptation is performed by interpolation of raster densification, according to one of four methods: nearest neighbour, Fashion 4 neighbours, bilinear interpolation and bicubic.</p>

    <p>- If geographic reference systems are different, there is a change in the system (the projection parameters, datum). In this case there will be an interpolation by one of four methods: nearest neighbour, Fashion 4 neighbours, bilinear interpolation or bicubic.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <p>The NoData value will be equal, as appropriate, to the value given by the user, if not beyond the range of raster data representation to adapt or, alternatively, the present value of the raster to adapt or However, if this is not defined, an implicit value that depends on the type of raster data to adapt as detailed below.</p>

  <div align="center">
    <table border="2" bordercolor="#000000" width="332">
      <tr>
        <th scope="col" width="162">Data Type</th>

        <th scope="col" width="160"><b>NoData Value</b></th>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>bit (logical)</td>

        <td>0</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>byte (character)</td>

        <td>255</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>integer (enter)</td>

        <td>-32768</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>long</td>

        <td>-2147483648</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td>real</td>

        <td>-3.4E+38</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div>
    <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%"/>
  </div>
  <exclusiva>
